From 81a42cf98986dc127797a0061b9b28a1f1d3d355 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:27:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] client: BADGE build, the app's own screens (pm3 --ui)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The design canvas "Proxmark3 app – ontwerp" built into the client, drawn
with the badge's libwb (why2025-linux/libwb, header-only; LIBWB= points at
it): Start, HF and LF, Search, a card type's actions, the MIFARE Classic
key check sector by sector with its dump, Cards with dump and keys,
Dictionary (which key lists Check keys tries; own lists open in Write),
Sniff (hf 14a sniff, then trace list -t mf) and a Console. In the client
itself so there is one process and one connection: a separate app next
to the client would not fit the memory pool.

client/src/badgeui/: pm3ui.c the screens, pm3ui_pm3.c what they ask the
client (commands with their output grabbed; the key check and block
reads through mifarehost.c), pm3ui_sim.c made-up answers for the host
test, gen_icons.py the icons and a 28 px mono font. proxmark3.c: --ui;
util.c: kbd_enter_pressed() asks the screens (Esc, Enter, the triangle).

Tested: test_pm3ui.py on the Mac (11 tests, ASan/UBSan). On the badge
(2026-10-30, RDV4 v4.21611 on J8, MIFARE Classic 1K 07 94 71 12) with
Tools/usb/hil/test_hil_pm3ui.py, 6 of 6: start from Apps and connect,
search (Gen 1a found), hf mf info, check keys 32/32, dump 64 blocks,
Dictionary, Console hw ping, sniff start and stop. bFLT 2.90 MB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
